<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bylazora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bylazora was the largest city of ancient Paeonia, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a> near modern Sveti Nikole in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>. It controlled the passes between Paeonia and Dardania, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> records that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a> captured it in 217 BCE. Excavations on the hill of Knezhje since 2008 have uncovered fortifications and buildings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> that many scholars identify with Bylazora.</p></div>
